As a Director of Operations, maintaining high-margin client relationships is the primary driver of firm stability. This project demonstrates a Predictive Operations Engine designed to identify "At-Risk" consulting clients before they terminate their contracts.

By integrating Heuristic AI Modeling with SQL Departmental Audits, this tool allowed for a strategic pivot in the Real Estate sector, identifying significant Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) currently sitting in the "Danger Zone."

🛠️ The Technical Stack
Python (Predictive Modeling): Developed a heuristic health-scoring algorithm to quantify client engagement and retention probability.

SQL (Aggregated Auditing): Performed cross-departmental analysis to identify industry-wide instability.

Tableau (Executive Dashboard): Created a live "Strategic Intervention Queue" to prioritize retention efforts for high-value accounts.

🚀 The "Health Score" Logic (AI Model)
The model assigns a health score (0-100) to every client based on three operational pillars:

Recency: Penalizes accounts with zero interaction for >30 days.

Engagement: Flags accounts where billables are high but engagement hours are low (The "Neglect" Signal).

Commitment: Rewards long-term (24-month) contract structures.

